From 1b317487d2f07dc6a423d7f28e57c3364c991df0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serhii Nikolaichuk <nikolaichuk.s.f@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:07:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] tacra: the RRP's verifiers, by name; a client certificate
 on every call; TLS 1.3

N24 (tacra-est 10-REQUIREMENTS-MATRIX, DR-B08; CVE-2026-92792): the backend no longer sends Evidence
to Veraison by default and to other verifiers by the TSM provider. Verifiers are named in the
configuration, each with the provider of the Evidence it appraises. Each RRP names the verifiers its
policy takes. In Passport the backend asks only those, the one for the Evidence's provider, and
refuses Evidence none of them appraises (403) before asking any verifier.

N23: the backend presents its client certificate (client_cert, client_key) to the RRPs and the
verifiers, over TLS 1.3. With the TACRA backend the EST server's own listener takes TLS 1.3 only,
as the reference implementation's server does (tacra-est BANK-PROFILE).

Tests: the RRP's verifier list, checked by mutating the routing; mutual TLS with an RRP that requires
a client certificate.
